adjudication.rationale:
In the diff, `Discourse.Group.findMembers` changed from returning a promise even when the group name is empty (`Ember.RSVP.resolve([])`) to `return;` (undefined):
```js
findMembers: function() {
  if (Em.isEmpty(this.get('name'))) { return ; }
  return Discourse.ajax(...)
}
```
This introduces an inconsistent return type (Promise vs undefined). Any caller that chains `findMembers().then(...)` to handle completion/empty results (as the old `afterModel` hooks did, and as other code may still do) would now throw when `name` is blank. That’s a concrete behavioral change/defect in the method’s contract introduced by the diff.
